routine les op=C4 mod=mem ea=q book="MOV DS0/DS1,reg16,memptr32" diff=m00:0,d8:0,d16:-1,dir:0 why="OPEN: book error where the measured routine is shorter than the book: (qprobe round 14, spec 10 B) LDS / LES r,mem is `P Y . D . U . D . . N .` (the qprobe lds / les runs, [BW]; the other modes by the measured heads): the heads (ea=q), the offset's read (Y + 3), D, a word, U (the segment's read posted), a word, D, two words, E with N; OPEN: the add, the offset's read, the address + 2 under the cycle, F: the register and the address register (00F8), the segment's read (00F9), F: DS1 on the E word (00FA): the book's EA + 17 with six book clocks with no act before the first post"
    bus=MEMR wid=WORD                       ; post the offset's read (Y + 3: a word)
    alu=INC2 ax=ADDR                        ; the address + 2 into SIGMA; the reservation (the second read)
    f wr=REG wid=WORD ws=OPR d1=ADDR s1=SIG ; D: F: the register <- the offset; the address register <- the address + 2
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 14) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1: the model's U is the post's word less one)
    bus=MEMR wid=WORD                       ; U: post the segment's read
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 14) a word with no act
    f wr=DS1 wid=WORD ws=OPR              ; D: F: DS1 <- the segment
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 14) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    e ro                                    ; E; N

